<title>TURKEY: Turk Petrol Ofisi Q1 profit up 96.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Petrol Ofisi Q1 profit up 96.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 1,030.92 vs     524.62</p>
<p>    Net profit		  2,597.92 vs   1,322.04</p>
<p>    Net sales		  95,849.68 vs  50,494.08</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  4,854.10 vs   2,125.99</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	3,600.80 vs   1,609.93</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense     2,462.45 vs   1,123.39</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   0    vs	 0</p>
<p>    Total debts		31,558.62 vs  15,843.31</p>
<p>    Equity		     12,925.13 vs   6,598.59</p>
<p>    Capital		     4,672.00 vs   4,672.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish petroleum products marketer and lubricants producer Petrol Ofisi A.S. is slated for privatisation with 93.3 percent of its capital held by the privatisation body OIB.</p>
<p>The company is in the process of raising its capital to seven trillion lira by issuing 1.3777 rights and 0.4 bonus for one existing share. It will pay a 2,726.5 lira dividend per 1,000 lira nominal valued share from 1996 profits at end-May.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
